 *
 * The class keeps an explicit 5-word chaining state plus a 64-byte residual
 * buffer, which makes `clone()` cheap.  HMAC exploits that: the ipad/opad
 * key blocks are compressed exactly once and every PRF call just clones the
 * resulting state instead of re-hashing the 64-byte key block.
